Description: libobs: a side by side canvas drawn once per eye, displays with two views
 The main canvas, when its layout is side by side (obs_set_video_stereo3d()), lays its scenes out in one eye's space
 (obs_get_video_eye_size(): the scene's own size, the canvas's for groups and nested scenes) and is drawn once per eye,
 each pass on its half of the canvas texture, with obs_get_render_eye() telling sources which eye is drawn: a flat
 source comes out the same in both eyes, at the screen plane; a source holding two views gives each eye its own.
 A texrender is drawn once per eye pass, so a filter or a transition never hands the right eye the left eye's picture.
 A display can hold two views side by side (obs_display_set_views()): its swap chain is twice as wide and its draw
 callbacks run once per eye on that eye's half, each given one view's size; viewports set while the swap chain is the
 target are relative to the view. In an eye pass the main canvas texture is drawn as that eye. New functions only; a
 2D canvas and a one-view display take the code paths they took before.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 61, milestone 3)
Forwarded: no, OBS asks for human-written submissions only (CONTRIBUTING.md, AI/Machine Learning Policy)
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
